"""Verified square-Hamilton-cycle generator for arXiv:2502.14794.

The solver receives a finite simple graph and must give a cyclic ordering whose
distance-one and distance-two pairs are all graph edges.  Generation samples
the cyclic ordering first, plants its square, adds near-threshold random edges,
and carries the ordering through a random relabelling.  No generated instance
